From 46bd22fddb040fc4c695d13ae371555c81430344 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:55:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] plan9/arm64: a port for 9front's arm64 kernel

The OS layer only (the arm64 compiler, assembler and linker are there):
- cmd/dist, internal/platform: plan9/arm64 a port (no cgo).
- cmd/link: 9front's arm64 a.out (7l -H2): R_MAGIC with the 64-bit
  header (40 bytes), text at 0x10000, data on the next 64K boundary
  (the kernel's R_MAGIC alignment).
- runtime: rt0, system calls (the number in R0, SVC, the arguments read
  by the kernel from 8(RSP) on in 8-byte slots), notes (sigtramp on the
  gsignal stack, noted; sigpanictramp pushes the faulting function's LR
  as signal_arm64.go's preparePanic does), the Ureg of /arm64/include/ureg.h;
  g lives in R28 only (no TLS: tls_arm64.h).
- syscall, cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/plan9: asm and zsyscall for arm64.
internal/cpu needs nothing: cpu_arm64_other.go reads no system registers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
